{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "169", "x": 0.895551985636664, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03819126296697169, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Part 3", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12334338960510077, "w": 0.07405254383377506, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Maya: So Finn, I've done as much as I can for our project on theater programs.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15360198182160828, "w": 0.8259341843109549, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "How's your research coming along?", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.173922722295561, "w": 0.372396852976038, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: Okay, Maya, I didn't know theater programs are called playbills in the USA", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.20418138995485352, "w": 0.8258514466732344, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "till I started looking into the topic. Even though I struggled to find many useful", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.22450213042880623, "w": 0.8258158705142642, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "websites, I'm glad we picked this subject. No one else on the course is doing the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2449711914181116, "w": 0.8267715056086788, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "same as us. Although it is one of the research areas of the module convenor.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2652919318920643, "w": 0.7824787775908748, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: That might actually put some people off, I suppose. So anyway, I hadn't", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2955876419588025, "w": 0.8259993901815748, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "realized there are actually companies specializing in creating theater programs.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3160567029481079, "w": 0.81940016648002, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: Yes, they're quite common nowadays. Contrary to what many people think,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3463152763039192, "w": 0.8260805899449882, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "theaters don't hire people to do the programs. In fact, companies buy the rights to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.36663601677787183, "w": 0.8262295587028666, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "publish programs on the theater's behalf and then make their money selling", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.38695675725182455, "w": 0.826011898225939, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "advertising space within the program booklet.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40742581824112994, "w": 0.47543386766263507, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: It must be easier for theaters to do it that way.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.43768441045763745, "w": 0.5479999021911941, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Finn: Yes, I remember reading something about programs in early British theater.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.46796774790763207, "w": 0.825932031286925, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "It said that the cast was always very important.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4882884883815848, "w": 0.4871250444573831, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: Yeah, audiences were very familiar with leading actors and big names", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5185471183194849, "w": 0.8265419522371099, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "would draw huge crowds.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5390161793087902, "w": 0.26899026146221294, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: But I hadn't realized that If the program named a famous actor, that's who", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5692748092466902, "w": 0.8259221888913597, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "the public expected to perform. And if that didn't happen, people accused the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5895955497206429, "w": 0.8260774116714202, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "theater of breaking their agreement with the audience. They would demand", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6099162524732031, "w": 0.8265646102519008, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "refunds, and if they didn't get them, there were riots.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.630385351183901, "w": 0.5449762875160592, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: Outrageous. That would never happen now.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6606809858078542, "w": 0.5175624476930502, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Finn: No. People are too polite. Even when they're disappointed, if the star of the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6909396534671467, "w": 0.8260579319301973, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "show misses a performance,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7112603939410994, "w": 0.29277576880130796, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: We should definitely include that information about early audiences in our", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7415189861576069, "w": 0.8262678005106358, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "project. I also think it's important to mention that lots of ordinary people at that", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7619880471469123, "w": 0.826011898225939, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "time were illiterate. So theater programs were of limited value in advertising", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.782308787620865, "w": 0.8260987368618117, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "plays. When a company of actors arrived in a town, they'd parade around the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8026295280948177, "w": 0.8263728885882857, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "streets in their costumes, beating drums and announcing their upcoming", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.823098589084123, "w": 0.826185780547592, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "performances.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8434193295580757, "w": 0.15787353710988103, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: Interesting. I couldn't imagine that happening now either.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8737026670080704, "w": 0.6458128091191435, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Maya: There's also an interesting comparison to make between 18th and 19th", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.903961334667363, "w": 0.8265773233461725, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "century programs. Finn: Wasn't it in the 19th century that theater programs", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9242819996985306, "w": 0.8260774116714202, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}